      "answer_text": "The plugin sends a heartbeat every **120,000 ms** (120 s). That is `HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS = 120_000` in `.opencode/plugins/context-engineering.ts`, around line 138.\n\n**Why it's needed:**\n- The bridge keeps a memory-only retention lease for each session. The source comment says the lease needs a sign of life within **300 s**.\n- A filtered result's `reference_id` has to stay readable through `retrieve_context`, possibly many turns and minutes later.\n- If nothing renews the lease, it lapses after 300 s and the reference expires after another 300 s (`.opencode/README.md`, \"Retention\").\n- 120 s is well inside the 300 s window, so one missed beat doesn't expire anything.\n\nThe timer sends `{type: \"heartbeat\", session_id}` for every session in the `liveSessions` set. A session joins that set in `tool.execute.after` or when `retrieve_context` runs, and leaves it on `session.deleted`. The timer is `unref`'d, so it doesn't keep the process alive.\n\nEvery other request for a session also renews its lease. The heartbeat covers long silences, such as a user pausing between turns."
    },
